hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17347","Haddathana al-Walid ibn Muslim, he said I heard Ibn Jabir saying: Haddathani Busr ibn Ubayd Allah al-Hadrami, that he heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Haddathani Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not pray toward graves, nor sit upon them."
"17348","Haddathana Attab ibn Ziyad, he said haddathana Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, my father said, and haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq, he said haddathana Abd Allah, he said haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, and he said haddathana Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, Ali said haddathana Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, he said I heard Abu Idris saying: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa saying: I heard Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not sit upon graves, nor pray over them."
